1 NAME Christina (Kristina) /Sandsmark/
2 GIVN Christina (Kristina)
2 SURN Sandsmark
2 _MARNM Lewison
2 NICK Christina (Kristina) Lewison (Sandsmark)
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 MAY 1828
2 PLAC Sønnmork Farm, Høle Annex, Strand Parish, Rogaland, Norway
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 APR 1866
2 ADDR
3 CITY Moscow
3 STAE WI
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lars used the last name of Lewison while married to Christina. They both came over on the ship from Norway in 1854. They were marring in 1856 or 1857 and had three children - Ingeborg (Belle) was the first born; 2 
2 CONC younger brothers died very early.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars and Christina lived on a farm near the present day Blanchardville, WI, until Lars was drafted into the 22nd regiment of the Wisconsin Infantry to do his part in the Civil War. It is unknown who helped Christina with the farm 
2 CONC work, but it may have been Ane as she was there when Christina died in 1866, less than a year after Lars mustered out of the arm on May 12, 1965.
