1 NAME Ole Johan Torjussen /Vig/
2 GIVN Ole Johan Torjussen
2 _MARNM Vig
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Greenwood Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Chimacum
3 STAE Washington
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 MAR 1908
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sinnes
3 STAE Vest-Agder
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 NOV 1958
2 ADDR
3 CITY Port Angeles
3 STAE WA
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb10411105191012 Født 1908] 
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/14553723/ole-johan-vig Find a grave] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra [https://wajcgs.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/2005_21_3.pdf Jefferson County Genealogical Society]: "Ole Johan Vig saw service in WWII where he was a Sgt with the 339 Service SQ A. A. F.  He was born March 25, 1908 and died N
2 CONC ovember 23, 1958"
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ole Johan Vig is listed in Volume 11, page 273.  His name is given as Vig, Ole J. birth date as 25 Mar 1908, birthplace, Norway, death day, 23 Nov., 1958; burial date, 29 Nov 1958; burial place, Greenwood cemetery.  He was not cr
2 CONC emated.  There is no listing for a spouse.  His father’s name was given as Torjus Zennes of Norway, his mother was Kristine Vig, no birthplace given.  He is listed as a veteran of WWII. His occupation was a brick mason from Rayoni
2 CONC er Co. of Port Angeles.",
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the Port Townsend Leader, 27 Nov 1958, it states, “Ole J. Vig Died While Out Hunting.”  He died of a heart attack after shooting and dressing a deer.  Funeral services were conducted by 
2 CONT Stroud’s Chapel, Port Townsend.  The article also states that he was born in Norway, March 25, 1908 and came to the U. S. as a child and lived with the Nailor family of Chimacum.  He moved to Port Angeles 20 years ago, working as 
2 CONC a mason with Rayonier Inc.  He served in the army during WWII and was a member of VFW Post 1024, Port Angeles.  His nearest survivor is an uncle, Ole Torkelson of Chimacum"
1 FAMC @F6000000021452368043@
1 RFN geni:6000000021452359625
