1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peder Andreas Pedersen (1831-after1905) of Log; Freight Man or "Fragtemand"; Bread Vendor or "Bagervend" (b. July 05, 1831, Log farm, Herad parish, Farsund, Vest-Agder, Norway - d. after 1905, Vanse parish, Farsund
2 CONC , Vest-Agder, Norway) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Peder Andreas Hansen (1790-1849) of Log; and Maren Sophia Olsdatter (1791-1868) of Gullestad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Peder was born on July 05, 1831 on Log Farm in Herad parish in Farsund, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: He was baptised under the name "Peder Andreas Pedersen" on July 17, 1831 at Herad parish in Farsund.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Pernille Helene Pedersdatter (1812) who died as an infant; Hans Pedersen (1814-1896) aka Hans Pedersen of Log who married Anne Marie Berntsdatter (1827-1884); Anna Pedersdatter (1816-1831); Olene Andrea Pedersdatter (181
2 CONC 9-1912) who married Villum Larsen (1816-1896) and had one of their children emigrate to the United States; Ole Mathias Pedersen (1822-1914), a baker who married Thea Johanne Torstensdatter (1825-1865); Helene Elisabeth Pedersdatte
2 CONC r (1825-?); Peder Pedersen (1829-1830) who died as an infant; and Hans Elias Pedersen (1837-?). All were baptised at Herad parish in Farsund.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Peder married Serine Larsdatter (1840-1905) of Drange, on July 26, 1862 at Herad parish in Farsund. Serine was the daughter of Lars Aadnessen. Peder was listed as "Peder Andreas Pederssen".
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Together they had the following children: Peder Elias Pedersen (1863-before1868); Lars Pedersen (1865) who was baptised on October 01, 1865; Lars Emanuel Pedersen (1869-?) who was baptised on July 18, 1869; Mathilde Soph
2 CONC ie Amalia Pedersen (1872-1949) aka Sophie Pedersen, who was baptised on Christmas Eve, December 24, 1872 and married Hans Andreas Carlsen Schultz (1867-1896), and after his death married Martin Andreassen (1865-c1935) and emigrate
2 CONC d with him to the United States with her daughters, Klara Helene Shultz (1895-1973), and Sigrid Marie Andreassen (1905-1940); Peder Severin Pedersen (1876-?) who was baptised on March 05, 1876; Anton Martin Teodore Pedersen (1879-
2 CONC ?) who was baptised on November 23, 1879; and Inga Karoline Eldora Pedersen (1882-1927) who was baptized on November 05, 1882 , and emigrated to New York in the United States, and married Emil Schneider (1884-1955). All the childr
2 CONC en were baptized in Farsund.
2 CONT
2 CONT Farsund, Norway: The family appears in the 1865 Norway Census living at 36 Kirkegaden in Farsund, where Peder was working as a freight man or "fragtemand". In the 1900 Norway Census he was living at 50b Nykastelgaden Street, Farsu
2 CONC nd, Vest-Agder, Norway and working as a "bagervend" or bread seller. Listed in the 1900 census were: Lars Emanuel Pedersen (1869-?) on a ship heading toward Vancouver, Canada, not married and working as a "styrmand" or sailor; Ped
2 CONC er Severin Pedersen (1876-?) who was on a ship heading toward "Arendal and Saint Petersburg, Russia", not married and working as a "matros", or sailor; and Anton Martin Teodore Pedersen (1879-?) who was on his way to Scotland, not
2 CONC  married and working as a "styrmand", or sailor. Missing from the census was Inga Pedersen who may have been working as a maid in another home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Wife: Serine died on October 06, 1905, and was buried on October 12, 1905. The churchbook lists her as: "baker's wife Serine Pedersen; [wife of] baker, Peder A. Pedersen; [she was] born 1840 [at] Drange in Herad."
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship: Peder Andreas Pedersen (1831-?) was the second, great-granduncle of Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ). He was the grandfather of Eddie August Schneider (1911-1940) the record breaking aviator. He was the great-grandfath
2 CONC er of Adelma Tandberg Steurer (1928- ); and June Tandberg Baker (1932- ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Researched and written by Richard Arthur Norton (1958- ) for Findagrave starting on November 12, 2004. 
2 CONT
